1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:45,980
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:48,400
=Episode 11=

4
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:10,980
This is my jade thumb ring.

5
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:13,290
For the rest of my life,

6
00:01:14,490 --> 00:01:15,980
I'll always protect you.

7
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:17,460
Rest and recover.

8
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:19,050
Wait for me to return.

9
00:01:19,690 --> 00:01:20,620
I'll take you to the palace.

10
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:02,290
Wanniang.

11
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:16,940
His Majesty met someone in secret

12
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:18,850
and stayed out all night.

13
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:24,780
(Concubine De)

14
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:34,730
Calm down, Your Highness.

15
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:39,220
A mere village woman
thinks she can rival me?

16
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:40,940
Let's see

17
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:42,980
if you live long enough

18
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:46,380
to set foot inside this palace.

19
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:52,730
Your Majesty.

20
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,100
Your Majesty, look at this.

21
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:08,380
What does this mean?

22
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:10,039
Your Majesty.

23
00:03:10,081 --> 00:03:12,380
I brought tonic to your chambers today.

24
00:03:12,890 --> 00:03:14,799
The sachet on your bed smelled of herbs,

25
00:03:14,841 --> 00:03:15,940
and I passed out.

26
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:19,100
When I woke, the imperial physician said
I'd been poisoned by those herbs.

27
00:03:19,290 --> 00:03:20,589
I'm very sensitive to medicine,

28
00:03:20,631 --> 00:03:21,730
so my symptoms were severe.

29
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:23,340
Your Majesty.

30
00:03:23,570 --> 00:03:24,570
You've been sleeping with it for days.

31
00:03:24,850 --> 00:03:26,690
I feared the toxins might build up,

32
00:03:26,890 --> 00:03:27,850
so I came to warn you.

33
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:29,690
Poisoned by those herbs?

34
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:30,220
Yes.

35
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:31,850
Your Majesty.

36
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:35,410
It contains asarum and raw pinellia.

37
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:37,380
Long exposure to asarum clouds the mind.

38
00:03:37,610 --> 00:03:38,980
Raw pinellia is highly toxic.

39
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:40,820
They counteract each other's toxicity
and aid sleep,

40
00:03:41,130 --> 00:03:43,540
but long-term use will harm your health.

41
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:51,100
Bring her in.

42
00:03:54,290 --> 00:03:56,540
Su Cao, how dare you!

43
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:59,850
You tried to poison His Majesty
with this vile sachet.

44
00:04:00,570 --> 00:04:01,540
I didn't.

45
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:02,980
Your Majesty.

46
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:04,730
You don't believe me?

47
00:04:10,610 --> 00:04:11,170
Your Majesty.

48
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:12,290
The evidence is clear.

49
00:04:12,610 --> 00:04:13,690
This vicious woman

50
00:04:13,890 --> 00:04:15,410
used a poisoned sachet to harm you.

51
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:16,730
She deserves to die!

52
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:17,799
Your Majesty.

53
00:04:17,841 --> 00:04:18,780
That's not true.

54
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:20,410
Wanniang didn't try to hurt you.

55
00:04:20,610 --> 00:04:21,319
That sachet...

56
00:04:21,361 --> 00:04:23,100
Wanniang risked her life to make it.

57
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:23,900
Qing'er.

58
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:25,220
Go on.

59
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:33,370
To make that sachet,

60
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:36,780
Wanniang mixed raw pinellia
with ginger juice and alum.

61
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:38,930
She left it out to collect dew
for seven nights.

62
00:04:39,170 --> 00:04:40,140
Then she steamed it.

63
00:04:40,610 --> 00:04:42,199
Each day, Wanniang turned the herbs over

64
00:04:42,241 --> 00:04:43,290
and tested their effects.

65
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:45,850
The raw pinellia's toxic sap
seeped into her skin.

66
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:47,850
At night, the pain was so bad

67
00:04:48,050 --> 00:04:49,780
she couldn't even lift her arm.

68
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,850
Yet she wouldn't let me tell you.

69
00:04:52,340 --> 00:04:53,140
Wanniang said

70
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:55,610
if Your Majesty could sleep well
for just one night,

71
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:58,050
she'd gladly endure any pain.

72
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:01,370
Imperial Physician Zhang.

73
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:03,100
Examine it.

74
00:05:24,610 --> 00:05:25,340
Your Majesty.

75
00:05:25,490 --> 00:05:27,100
The raw pinellia in this sachet

76
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:29,020
was indeed treated with ginger and alum,

77
00:05:29,250 --> 00:05:30,140
then left out for seven nights.

78
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:31,250
Its toxicity

79
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:32,900
has been reduced by 90 percent.

80
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:34,050
However,

81
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:35,410
the person who made the sachet

82
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:36,639
stayed by the stove each day,

83
00:05:36,681 --> 00:05:37,700
breathing in medicinal fumes.

84
00:05:37,850 --> 00:05:38,730
Residual toxins entered her lungs

85
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:40,020
and spread upward through her meridians,

86
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:42,290
causing blue lines to appear on her arm.

87
00:05:42,810 --> 00:05:44,020
Everything this young woman said

88
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:45,460
is true.

89
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:09,830
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

90
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:14,030
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

91
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:17,270
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

92
00:06:17,590 --> 00:06:19,340
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

93
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:23,240
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

94
00:06:24,070 --> 00:06:27,230
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

95
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:31,590
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

96
00:06:32,510 --> 00:06:34,840
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

97
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:37,020
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

98
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:40,270
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

99
00:06:41,270 --> 00:06:44,420
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

100
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:49,470
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

101
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:52,300
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

102
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:56,650
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

103
00:06:58,110 --> 00:07:01,240
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

104
00:07:01,290 --> 00:07:06,470
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

105
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:14,820
♪The past has faded away♪

106
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:18,880
♪The past has faded away♪
